{"repositoryId":1094352151,"availability":"available","full":"ObayM/math-concepts","name":"math-concepts","description":"Explore this public GitHub project.","category":"Other","language":"TypeScript","stars":1,"forks":0,"created":"2025-11-11T15:42:58Z","updated":"2026-10-14T19:22:43Z","branch":"main","homepage":"https://math-concepts.vercel.app","topics":[],"demo":"https://math-concepts.vercel.app/","color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-16T15:52:16.915Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-16T15:52:16.915Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-16T15:52:16.915Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-16T15:52:16.915Z","stars":1,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Mathly is live but still early and the Arabic side is still far from complete!","I always liked math but it was hard for others to understand it, and for me sometimes. The problem with traditional math is it's just reading or listening to a teacher explain it on a whiteboard, which might not click with everyone. Thanks to people like 3Blue1Brown who inspired some of this.","So I built a platform where it's all based on interactivity. I've been using it myself to teach myself some of the math I get in school. You drag a point along a curve and watch the tangent follow. You build an equation one piece at a time. You sketch a graph before the answer is revealed. When you get something wrong, the lesson doesn't just say \"try again\", it takes a detour to walk you through exactly what you missed, then puts you back where you were."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/ObayM/math-concepts/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"432eb6e0846de706e0bc4df0f715ff9e228e1fcc30cdc443d38ee4649adbd4f2","extractedAt":"2026-10-16T15:52:17.048Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-16T15:52:17.048Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Mathly is live but still early and the Arabic side is still far from complete!","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/ObayM/math-concepts/blob/main